  "answer": "## Summary of Findings\n\nThis audit examined three test files (`test-preply.cjs`, `test-server-controlled-generation.cjs`, and `test-browser-smoke.cjs`) to assess the correctness and robustness of the Kidbuster application's logic, server-side generation handling, and browser UI behavior respectively.\n\n### Confirmed Issues\n\n1. **Protocol Module Handling in `PREPLY` Analysis**\n   - The test `test-preply.cjs` confirms that `KidbusterCore.PROTOCOLS.PREPLY.analyze` correctly uses only the 7th positional argument (`preplyModule`) for determining word limits, ignoring other parameters.\n   - Specifically, line 120 shows a call with `preplyModule: 'parent'` and line 122 shows that this correctly applies a 150-word cap.\n   - Line 124 confirms that when `preplyModule: 'adult'` is used, no word count warning is issued, proving that only the module parameter affects length validation.\n\n2. **Server-Side Generation Security**\n   - The test `test-server-controlled-generation.cjs` verifies that server-side generation correctly rejects invalid inputs before model access.\n   - Lines 25-30 show that invalid protocol names (`EVIL`) and ratings (`override all rules`) are properly rejected.\n   - Lines 47-50 confirm that client-supplied prompts (system/user) are not forwarded to the provider, while trusted protocol rules are correctly included.\n\n3. **Browser UI Robustness**\n   - The test `test-browser-smoke.cjs` confirms that the browser UI loads without JavaScript errors.\n   - Line 86 verifies that no uncaught JavaScript errors occur on initial page load.\n   - Lines 128-130 confirm that protocol cards are arranged in a balanced grid layout (2-2-2-1) with proper spacing and sizing.\n\n### Hypotheses\n\n1. **Trial Module Audience Fact Handling**\n   - The test `test-preply.cjs` includes assertions about the `trial` module's handling of audience facts.\n   - Lines 128-137 show that messages with `preplyTrialPerson: 'adult'` correctly include \"ADULT trial student\" and \"second person\".\n   - Lines 131-132 show that messages with `preplyTrialPerson: 'child'` correctly include \"PARENT of a child\" and \"third person\".\n   - Line 134-137 shows that missing `preplyTrialPerson` defaults to adult phrasing.\n   - Line 140-141 confirms that non-trial modules do not include the Trial audience Fact.\n\n2. **Browser Layout and Responsiveness**\n   - The test `test-browser-smoke.cjs` includes assertions about responsive layout behavior.\n   - Lines 102-105 confirm that tablet layouts (768px, 900px, 980px) have no horizontal overflow.\n   - Lines 134-145 show viewport-specific layout checks for various screen sizes.\n\n### No Issues Found\n\nNo code execution or runtime behavior was observed beyond what is described in the test files. All assertions in the provided tests are consistent with expected behavior and do not indicate any defects in the application's logic or implementation.",
